and then fire to v3 , as shown in Fig. 2d . Notice that we have returned back to the initial hunger
state h = 0, so this process repeats, visiting states 1, 2, 3, then back to 1, and so on. Notice that
we fire the chip from 3 to 1 even though P31 = 0.
   If one ignores the chip and focuses on the entries of the hunger vector, the hunger game can be
viewed as a greedy variant of chip-firing. Specifically, if all entries of h and P are rational, we can
