our claim is false, and let k be the smallest index for which the claim fails, so that hi < −1 for
some i. Consider the set S of states whose hunger changed during the hunger game process from
h(0) to h(k) ; this set must be finite, for each of the k steps can only change the hunger of finitely
many states, and must contain i. The total hunger of this set must be constant during this hunger
